hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2835","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Isa, narrated to us Nu'aym ibn Hammad, narrated to us 'Isa ibn Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja'far—who is Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Husayn—on the authority of Jabir (RA), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during his Farewell Pilgrimage ordered a caller to announce, and he called out at midday: \Perform ghusl (ritual bath).\"" He then mentioned the hadith at length and said:\n\n\""Then when the Day of Tarwiyah came"","" the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered a caller"","" who announced: 'Make the talbiyah for Hajj.' He also ordered that the sacrificial camels (budn) be made to stand at 'Arafah"","" and this applied to all the rites.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
